{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Expose node1's staged projects directory as an authenticated, writable SMB share named projects for the design team.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node1's final Samba configuration exposes only the projects share at the required path, limits access to the design group, and is writable. The service is enabled, active, listening on SMB ports, and remotely visible from node2.","evidence_ids":["cmd-1badeb400c194e01","cmd-d563b87d6b524501","cmd-94679782e73f438d"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Node2 can list, read, and update documents as designer using the demonstration credentials.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node2 authenticated as designer, listed the share, read the original drawing, created and replaced a document, and verified the updated content by round trip. These operations also succeeded after both restarts. The credential value is redacted, but the captured access.txt inspection identifies designer as the demonstration account and subsequent authentication succeeds.","evidence_ids":["cmd-dc2d65e5233d41b2","cmd-d563b87d6b524501","cmd-e0558f6a649a4438","cmd-231f3d1906114968"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Reject guest access to the projects share.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Unauthenticated tree connections were directly rejected with NT_STATUS_ACCESS_DENIED before and after the node restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d563b87d6b524501","cmd-a26f87127f0843b5","cmd-e0558f6a649a4438"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Reject access to sibling directories.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The private sibling was not exported as a share, authenticated access to //node1/private failed, and traversal from projects toward private/contracts.txt was rejected. The final configuration contains only projects and disables symlink following.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d563b87d6b524501","cmd-e0558f6a649a4438","cmd-94679782e73f438d"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Keep the initial drawings in /srv/legacy2/samba-team-share intact.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Final SHA-256 hashes for drawing.txt and materials.csv exactly match the prepared baseline, including after the SMB updates and node restarts.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-74136aeea0a948e6","cmd-987065c608ef4103","cmd-94679782e73f438d"]},{"id":"R6","requirement":"Retain the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained on Ubuntu 16.04.7 with kernel 4.4.0-210-generic. Ubuntu Xenial's Samba/smbclient 4.3.11 packages were installed, and package consistency remained healthy.","evidence_ids":["global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_prepare:node2:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform","cmd-94679782e73f438d","cmd-231f3d1906114968","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.96,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.84,"summary":"Core mutations—package installation, account/group creation, permissions, Samba configuration, document updates, and mandated restarts—were causally connected to the outcome or its verification. The restart protocol was strong on both nodes: healthy pre-state, acknowledgement/disruption, changed boot IDs, recovered systems, persistent data, and successful post-restart SMB behavior; fixed lifecycle boot identities independently agree. Two low-risk retained package mutations were unnecessary in the demonstrated implementation: smbclient was explicitly installed on node1 but never used there (cmd-031f39c2536d435c), and cifs-utils was explicitly installed on node2 but no CIFS mount was used (cmd-82fb4e2e4cf64ff5). Node2 also retained six bounded evidence artifacts in /tmp from final testing rather than cleaning them: five from cmd-e0558f6a649a4438 and one from cmd-231f3d1906114968. These artifacts supported verification but constitute minor final residue. No failed services or damaged package state were observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-031f39c2536d435c","cmd-82fb4e2e4cf64ff5","cmd-e0558f6a649a4438","cmd-231f3d1906114968","cmd-2f5bc5437fa2497b","cmd-275c714815e34318","cmd-746c92d782264abd","cmd-da4e287114fe4f13","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct client/server behavioral evidence. The SMB share remained functional and protected after both managed nodes were restarted, and the original drawing contents, OS release, and kernel were preserved. Hygiene is reduced modestly by two unused explicitly installed client packages and uncleaned node2 test artifacts.","limitations":["The secret values are redacted, so the exact password cannot be compared textually between access.txt and the SMB commands; successful designer authentication and the captured demonstration-account inspection provide indirect linkage.","The fixed after-executor listening-socket observation is empty even though direct final node1 commands show smbd listening on ports 139 and 445. Direct post-restart service and remote-client behavior outweigh this collector inconsistency."]}
